From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:45:07 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] segacd-discs

A Sega CD game of several discs is one game, the PS1 way (ADR 0067):
discs named (Disc N) with no playlist get a generated one in
Config/playlists/SEGACD, the discs a playlist names leave the shelf,
SELECT+L2 swaps to the next disc with a banner, Saves/SEGACD/<stem>.disc
remembers the disc, and a state carries the disc it was taken on in the
same trailer as PS1. Three things differ, because Genesis Plus GX:

- joins every m3u line to the playlist's own directory, so a Sega CD
  playlist holds paths relative to itself
  (../../../Games/SEGACD/<disc>), where PS1 playlists keep absolute ones;
- offers only the legacy disk control interface, with no
  set_initial_image, so a remembered disc is swapped in right after the
  load instead of being handed to the core before it;
- holds 4 discs.

The disc file helpers and the playlist tidy now take the platform; PS1
keeps its paths, its absolute playlists and its behaviour.
